#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:2
msgid "Serialization and Hashing"
msgstr "Serialización y hashing"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:4
msgid ""
"Almost every object in QiliSDK can be written to disk and read back, and "
"every object that takes part in symbolic expressions needs a hash that "
"stays the same across processes. Both of these are provided by "
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.serialization`."
msgstr ""
"Casi todos los objetos de QiliSDK pueden escribirse en disco y volver a "
"leerse, y todo objeto que participe en expresiones simbólicas necesita un"
" hash que se mantenga igual entre procesos. "
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.serialization` proporciona ambas cosas."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:9
msgid "Serialization"
msgstr "Serialización"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:11
msgid ""
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.serialization` offers four entry-points, built on the"
" YAML handler in :mod:`qilisdk.yaml`:"
msgstr ""
":mod:`qilisdk.utils.serialization` ofrece cuatro puntos de entrada, "
"construidos sobre el gestor de YAML de :mod:`qilisdk.yaml`:"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:14
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.serialize` — serialize an object to a"
" YAML string."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.serialize` — serializar un objeto en "
"una cadena YAML."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:15
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.serialize_to` — serialize an object "
"to a YAML file."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.serialize_to` — serializar un objeto "
"en un archivo YAML."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:16
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.deserialize` — rebuild an object from"
" a YAML string."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.deserialize` — reconstruir un objeto "
"a partir de una cadena YAML."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:17
msgid ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.deserialize_from` — rebuild an object"
" from a YAML file."
msgstr ""
":func:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.deserialize_from` — reconstruir un "
"objeto a partir de un archivo YAML."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:27
msgid "**Output**::"
msgstr "**Salida**::"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:44
msgid ""
"Each ``!Tag`` in the output names the class that produced the node, which"
" allows the object graph to be rebuilt exactly."
msgstr ""
"Cada ``!Tag`` de la salida nombra la clase que produjo el nodo, lo que "
"permite reconstruir exactamente el grafo de objetos."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:47
msgid "Writing to and reading from a file works in the same way:"
msgstr "Escribir en un archivo y leer de él funciona de la misma forma:"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:63
msgid "Checking the type on the way back"
msgstr "Comprobar el tipo a la vuelta"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:65
msgid ""
"Both ``deserialize`` functions accept an optional class as their second "
"argument. When given, the rebuilt object is checked against it and the "
"call is typed as returning that class."
msgstr ""
"Ambas funciones ``deserialize`` aceptan una clase opcional como segundo "
"argumento. Si se indica, el objeto reconstruido se comprueba contra ella "
"y la llamada queda tipada como si devolviera esa clase."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:76
msgid "Errors"
msgstr "Errores"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:78
msgid "Failures are wrapped so that callers only have to catch two exceptions:"
msgstr ""
"Los fallos se envuelven para que quien llama solo tenga que capturar dos "
"excepciones:"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:80
msgid ""
":class:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.SerializationError` — the object "
"could not be written."
msgstr ""
":class:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.SerializationError` — no se pudo "
"escribir el objeto."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:81
msgid ""
":class:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.DeserializationError` — the YAML "
"could not be parsed, or the result is not an instance of the requested "
"class."
msgstr ""
":class:`~qilisdk.utils.serialization.DeserializationError` — no se pudo "
"analizar el YAML, o el resultado no es una instancia de la clase "
"solicitada."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:84
msgid "Registering your own classes"
msgstr "Registrar tus propias clases"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:86
msgid ""
"A class becomes serializable by registering it with the shared YAML "
"handler. The decorator assigns the tag automatically from the class name,"
" and every public QiliSDK class that you can serialize uses it:"
msgstr ""
"Una clase se vuelve serializable al registrarla en el gestor de YAML "
"compartido. El decorador asigna la etiqueta automáticamente a partir del "
"nombre de la clase, y todas las clases públicas de QiliSDK que puedes "
"serializar lo usan:"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:99
msgid ""
"Pass ``shared=True`` to prefix the tag with the top-level package name, "
"which avoids collisions with tags defined elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"Pasa ``shared=True`` para anteponer a la etiqueta el nombre del paquete "
"de nivel superior, lo que evita colisiones con etiquetas definidas en "
"otro sitio."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:104
msgid ""
"The handler is a ruamel ``YAML(typ=\"unsafe\")`` instance, so "
"deserializing constructs arbitrary Python objects named in the document. "
"Only load files you trust."
msgstr ""
"El gestor es una instancia ``YAML(typ=\"unsafe\")`` de ruamel, así que "
"deserializar construye objetos de Python arbitrarios nombrados en el "
"documento. Carga solo archivos en los que confíes."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:108
msgid "Hashing"
msgstr "Hashing"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:110
msgid ""
":func:`qilisdk.utils.hashing.hash` produces a stable hash for the objects"
" QiliSDK builds expressions out of. It is used by "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.variables.BaseVariable`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Expression`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.qtensor.QTensor`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.Hamiltonian`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.digital.circuit.Circuit` and the gates, so that terms "
"can be collected in dictionaries and compared reliably."
msgstr ""
":func:`qilisdk.utils.hashing.hash` produce un hash estable para los "
"objetos con los que QiliSDK construye expresiones. Lo usan "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.variables.BaseVariable`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Expression`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.qtensor.QTensor`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.analog.hamiltonian.Hamiltonian`, "
":class:`~qilisdk.digital.circuit.Circuit` y las puertas, de modo que los "
"términos pueden agruparse en diccionarios y compararse de forma fiable."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:122
msgid "It differs from Python's built-in ``hash`` in two main ways:"
msgstr ""
"Se diferencia del ``hash`` integrado de Python en dos aspectos "
"principales:"

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:124
msgid ""
"It is **stable across processes**. Python randomizes string hashing per "
"interpreter run, whereas this one is a `blake2b "
"<https://www.blake2.net/>`_ digest of a canonical encoding, so the same "
"object hashes to the same integer every time."
msgstr ""
"Es **estable entre procesos**. Python aleatoriza el hash de las cadenas "
"en cada ejecución del intérprete, mientras que este es un resumen "
"`blake2b <https://www.blake2.net/>`_ de una codificación canónica, así "
"que el mismo objeto produce siempre el mismo entero."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:125
msgid ""
"It is **consistent across numeric types**. Values are encoded as exact "
"integer ratios, so ``1``, ``1.0`` and ``(1+0j)`` all hash alike, and "
"``nan``, ``inf`` and NumPy scalars are handled explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Es **coherente entre tipos numéricos**. Los valores se codifican como "
"razones exactas de enteros, de modo que ``1``, ``1.0`` y ``(1+0j)`` "
"producen el mismo hash, y ``nan``, ``inf`` y los escalares de NumPy se "
"tratan explícitamente."

#: ../../modules/utils/utils_serialization.rst:129
msgid ""
"The returned integer is compatible with Python's ``__hash__`` protocol, "
"so it can be returned directly from a ``__hash__`` method. It is not a "
"cryptographic commitment and should not be used as one."
msgstr ""
"El entero devuelto es compatible con el protocolo ``__hash__`` de Python,"
" así que puede devolverse directamente desde un método ``__hash__``. No "
"es un compromiso criptográfico y no debe usarse como tal."

